    "created_at": "2022-04-29T06:57:11Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-04-29T06:57:11Z",
    "body": "@jimmywarting two things:\r\n\r\n1. Commenting on closed issues rarely works as they tend to get ignored in triage.\r\n2. It's not really clear to me what a couple of downvotes signifies. If you want a feature like this, showing there's demand for it through successful libraries, Stack Overflow questions, etc. would be much more viable. And Open UI would probably be a good place to start a productive conversation about that.",
